A voice box is a small wooden box about the size of a baseball, most of its sides plain unfinished wood, with a grate on the front like a speaker and a small button on one side beside it. The [[Org/Friends of Aut|Friends of Aut]] keep a shelf of them in the threshold room of the [[Pharos]] and let each group take one before crossing into the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]]. The box does not resonate. It is part of the ritual of that place: sounds are caught and put somewhere else with it. It grows warm near a sound worth catching, as it did near the moth in the driver's cab at Vermillion Square Station.
